    <!-- ★ Absent cellular has to be stated, not merely omitted.
         Measured on the flash-2 boot: eight warnings, every boot, one per key —

           W ModemPowerProfile: getAverageBatteryDrainMaH called with unexpected
             key: 0x10000000, drain:IDLE,RAT:DEFAULT      (and SLEEP, RX, TX 0-4)

         PowerProfile.initModem() (:836-859) calls handleDeprecatedModemConstant()
         for those eight keys UNCONDITIONALLY — there is no "does this device have
         a modem" branch anywhere on that path. Each call asks
         ModemPowerProfile.getAverageBatteryDrainMa(key) first, and :498 logs the
         warning whenever the key is missing. Leaving the section out does not opt
         out of the lookups; it only guarantees all eight of them miss.

         ⚠️ This changes NO computed value. Without the block,
         handleDeprecatedModemConstant falls back to getAveragePower(
         "modem.controller.*"), which is also absent, so it returns the caller's
         default of 0 and stores 0.0. With the block, the same eight constants are
         0 because they say so. Identical end state, eight fewer log lines, and the
         intent is now written down in the file that BatteryStats actually reads
         rather than only in the comment at the top.

         <active> carries no rat= attribute on purpose: getTypeFromAttribute
         (:346-352) returns 0 for an absent attribute, and MODEM_RAT_TYPE_DEFAULT
         is 0 — which is exactly the key initModem() looks up. Five transmit
         levels because MODEM_TX_LEVEL_COUNT is 5 (:151); a sixth would be
         rejected with "Unexpected tx level" and a missing one would leave that
         key NaN, i.e. the warning back again for that level only. -->
    <modem>
        <sleep>0</sleep>
        <idle>0</idle>
        <active>
            <receive>0</receive>
            <transmit level="0">0</transmit>
            <transmit level="1">0</transmit>
            <transmit level="2">0</transmit>
            <transmit level="3">0</transmit>
            <transmit level="4">0</transmit>
        </active>
    </modem>
